# Integrate Site Readiness Backend APIs

This plan outlines the approach to integrate the completed Site Readiness backend APIs into the `fleet-insights-pro` frontend, replacing the current mock data implementation.

## Frontend Architecture Analysis
Based on the inspection of the repository, the frontend is built using the following conventions:
- **Framework:** React 19 with TanStack Start (SSR) and Vite as the bundler.
- **Folder Structure:** Feature-based routing in `src/routes/`, reusable components in `src/components/`, and business logic/API wrappers in `src/lib/`.
- **Routing Pattern:** File-based routing via `@tanstack/react-router`. Site Readiness already has routes set up (`readiness.tsx`, `readiness.index.tsx`, `readiness.ops.tsx`, `readiness.config.tsx`).
- **API Service Pattern:** Native `fetch` wrappers defined in `src/lib/<module>/api.ts` (as seen in `mis/api.ts`).
- **State Management:** `@tanstack/react-query` is installed and ideal for server state. Currently, readiness uses a local storage store (`src/lib/readiness-store.ts`) and mock data (`readiness-data.ts`). We will transition from local storage to React Query.
- **Validation Pattern:** `zod` and `react-hook-form` are used for robust form validation.
- **UI Components:** Built on Tailwind CSS v4 and Radix UI primitives (shadcn/ui style), utilizing `Table`, `Dialog`, `Form`, `Select`, etc., with `sonner` for toast notifications.
- **Config/Env:** No explicit `.env` file exists yet for API bases. We will need to define one.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Backend URL:** The plan assumes the FastAPI backend is running locally at `http://localhost:8000`. Is this the correct base URL?
> **Mock Data Deprecation:** The current `readiness-store.ts`, `readiness-data.ts`, and `readiness-config.ts` will be deprecated or heavily refactored to consume the live API instead of local storage.

